# Files excluded from the archive uploaded to EAS Build.
#
# =============================================================================================
# 🛑 THIS FILE REPLACES .gitignore — IT IS NOT ADDITIVE
# =============================================================================================
# eas-cli's Ignore class (eas-cli 22.0.0, build/vcs/local.js:49-59) is explicit:
#
#     * - if .easignore exists, .gitignore files are not used.
#
#     if (await fs.pathExists(easIgnorePath)) {
#       this.ignoreMapping = [['', ignore().add(defaultIgnore)],
#                             ['', ignore().add(await fs.readFile(easIgnorePath, 'utf-8'))]];
#       return;                       // <-- never reads any .gitignore, root or nested
#     }
#
# and `defaultIgnore` for copying is only `.git` + `node_modules` (local.js:33-36).
#
# eas.json sets no `requireCommit`, so it defaults to false, and with requireCommit false
# eas-cli SHALLOW-COPIES THE WORKING DIRECTORY rather than exporting a git commit
# (build/vcs/clients/git.js:199-207). Untracked files therefore ship too.
#
# Consequence: the moment this file was created, every .gitignore rule in the repo stopped
# applying to the upload — including `*.p8` in apps/mobile/.gitignore, which covers
# apps/mobile/AuthKey_R9QZ5LP8NK.p8, the App Store Connect private key that the mobile
# workflows write to disk immediately before `eas build` runs. That key, plus every build
# artifact and any .env file present on the runner, was being uploaded to Expo.
#
# So this file restates .gitignore first, and only then adds the EAS-specific exclusions.
# 🛑 If you add a rule to .gitignore that protects a secret, add it here too.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Restated from the ROOT .gitignore
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/dist
